1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
I would start paying attention about how I present myself now.
我会开始留意自己如何展现自己。

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,789
This has a lot to do with perception because right now as we're fast tracking oursel in this one month.
这与他人的观感很有关系，因为现在我们正想在这一个月内加快成长。

3
00:00:08,799 --> 00:00:19,120
How people perceive us and how the world perceives us doing certain things is going to be positively correlated with what we get from said people said audiences said boss whatever it may be.
她认为，别人和世界如何看待我们的行动，会与我们从相关人、受众或老板那里得到的回应呈正相关。

4
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,160
So right now if you're a person who's like I don't care what anyone thinks about me.
如果你现在觉得，我不在乎别人怎么看我——

5
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:26,960
I don't care how I show up I don't care about how I look all these different things great that's amazing.
我不在乎自己的表现，也不在乎外表，等等，她说，这很好。

6
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:34,400
But also what if you took one month to actually care how you were perceived or actually care how you presented yourself and see where that gets you.
但如果花一个月在乎别人怎样看你，或在乎你如何展现自己，再看看结果如何呢？

7
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:39,680
Especially if you're working towards something that maybe is a relationship or something in the work space.
尤其当你正朝着某个目标努力，例如一段关系或工作方面的目标时。

8
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:45,120
How people perceive you is exactly how they treat you and is sometimes going to give you what you want.
她认为，别人如何看待你，就会如何对待你，有时也会因此给你想要的东西。

9
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:52,000
So if you do not care about the way you present yourself if you do not care about the way that you take care of yourself no one else will you know what I'm saying.
她说，如果自己都不在乎如何展现和照顾自己，也不会有别人来在乎，明白我的意思吗？

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,510
But for that one month I would start caring more about the way that I took care of myself and the way that I presented myself to the world.
但在这一个月里，我会更在乎如何照顾自己，以及如何向世界展现自己。

11
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:01,680
Because I want the world to know that I take care of me so you better take care of me.
因为我想让世界知道，我照顾自己，所以你也最好好好对待我。

12
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:06,320
It gets so much deeper than that it even goes into the way that we talk the way that we communicate with people.
这还有更深的含义，甚至涉及我们说话和与人沟通的方式。

13
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:11,359
I want to be perceived as someone who is confident I want to be perceived as someone who knows what they're talking about.
我希望被看作一个有自信的人，也希望被看作一个懂自己在说什么的人。

14
00:01:11,359 --> 00:01:18,640
I want to be perceived because that is going to be directly affecting my business and the relationships that I develop and whatever I may have.
我希望自己的形象得到认可，因为那会直接影响我的业务、建立的关系以及其他方面。

15
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:27,110
So I need to take care of myself to show whoever I'm trying to get something from I am capable I am worthy and I got this.
所以我需要照顾自己，向我想获得回应的人表明：我有能力，我值得，我能行。

16
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:31,190
You got this the last thing that I would do is I would keep my space clean.
你也能行。我最后会做的一件事，是保持自己的生活空间整洁。

17
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:38,160
This is your house this is your room whatever areas that you were in because your mind is a representation of your living space.
这可以是你的房子、房间或你待的地方，因为她认为人的心境是居住空间的反映。

18
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:42,799
So if your living space is messy if you are keeping your room a mess you're like oh I'll get to it on sunday.
如果居住空间很乱，房间一直乱着，而你说周日再来处理——

19
00:01:42,799 --> 00:01:48,960
And you're not doing little cleanings here and there while you can and cleaning up after yourself directly you are doing yourself a disservice.
但平时有时间却不随手清理，也不及时收拾自己的东西，她认为这是亏待自己。

20
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:52,880
You want your space your living space to be clear so that way when you think of ideas.
你希望自己的生活空间保持清爽，这样当你思考点子时——

21
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:57,830
The ideas are coming from a place of not of stress not of being overwhelmed but from a clean slate.
点子就不是来自压力和不堪重负，而是像从一张干净白纸般的状态中产生。

22
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:02,080
Your house is your slate the least you can do is keep your space clean.
她说，你的家就是那块白板，你最起码可以保持空间整洁。

23
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:08,239
Because that is your base for going into the world that is your base for your creativity that is your base for how far you will go.
因为那是你走向世界的基础，是创造力的基础，也是你能走多远的基础。

24
00:02:08,239 --> 00:02:11,760
Cuz if you can't even take care of your home how can you take care of something bigger than you.
她反问，因为如果连自己的家都照顾不好，又怎能照顾比自己更大的事情？

25
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:15,039
Be really intentional about how you keep your space in this one month.
在这一个月里，要很有意识地安排和维护自己的生活空间。

26
00:02:15,039 --> 00:02:21,919
If you really want to kickstart and push yourself be so intentional about how you keep your space because everything that you do is compounded.
如果真的想启动改变、推动自己，就认真维护空间，因为她说你做的每件事都会不断积累。

27
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:25,830
Everything that you do adds up to the person that you are when people are not looking.
你做的每件事，会累积成那个在无人注视时的你。

28
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:29,190
The way that you treat things and how you do things is how you do everything.
她认为，你如何对待事物、如何做事，就体现了你做所有事情的方式。

29
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:32,000
I don't care how good and how clean you are in the office.
我不在乎你在办公室看起来多好、多整洁。

30
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,479
If I go to your home and your home is a wreck I'm like this is not who she is.
如果到你家，发现家里一团糟，我就会觉得，这和她展现的样子不一致。

31
00:02:36,479 --> 00:02:40,239
You want the person that you are at home and the person that you are in the office to be aligned.
你希望在家的自己和在办公室的自己是一致的。

32
00:02:40,239 --> 00:02:46,080
You want it to be who you really are you want to start showing up in spaces as you and that starts in your home.
你希望这是真实的自己，希望以真实的自己出现在各种场合，而这从家里开始。

33
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:49,840
Now you've got one month to change your life you've got one month to develop yourself.
现在，你有一个月改变生活，有一个月发展自己。

34
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:56,880
And this should be such a great base for anyone who doesn't know where to start what to look at how to start making these small changes in your life.
她认为，对不知道从哪里开始、关注什么，或怎样在生活中做小改变的人来说，这些应该是很好的基础。

35
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:00,160
These are going to be so beneficial to you on your self development journey.
她说，这些做法会在个人成长过程中带来很多帮助。

36
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:03,520
And again be easy with yourself but also get real with yourself.
再说一次，对自己温柔些，但也要诚实面对自己。

37
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:07,520
It is great to rest when you need to rest it is so great to go hard when you need to go hard.
需要休息时休息很好，需要努力时认真努力也很好。

38
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,640
But you also need to be honest with yourself and straightforward.
但你也需要对自己诚实，直截了当。

39
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:17,680
If you keep falling back because you're not staying consistent with the things that you want in life and the things that you tell yourself you're going to do.
如果总是退回原处，因为没有持续做生活中想做的事，也没坚持履行自己说过要做的事——

40
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:20,320
Get up get back up get back on the saddle keep going.
那就起来，再站起来，重新上马，继续前进。

41
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:23,440
Because you only have one life and you want to make it the best life that you possibly can.
因为人生只有一次，你想尽可能把它过好。
